            {
              "id": "EL-PE-027",
              "name": "PassARoleToANewSageMakerNotebook",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Pass a role to a new SageMaker notebook"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pass a role to a new SageMaker notebook. Scope iam:PassRole to the roles the caller must pass and add \"Condition\": {\"StringEquals\": {\"iam:PassedToService\": \"sagemaker.amazonaws.com\"}} only for those roles."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/brennocm/escalint/blob/main/docs/rules/EL-PE-027.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Pass a role to a new SageMaker notebook\n\nRemediation: Scope iam:PassRole to the roles the caller must pass and add \"Condition\": {\"StringEquals\": {\"iam:PassedToService\": \"sagemaker.amazonaws.com\"}} only for those roles.",
                "markdown": "# EL-PE-027 — Pass a role to a new SageMaker notebook\n\n| | |\n| --- | --- |\n| Severity | high (critical when the edge is on a path to Tier 0) |\n| Category | new-passrole |\n| Status | stable |\n| Edge | `passrole_compute` |\n| Required actions | `iam:PassRole`, `sagemaker:CreateNotebookInstance` |\n| pathfinding.cloud | [sagemaker-001](https://pathfinding.cloud/paths/aws/sagemaker-001) |\n\n## Description\n\nThe principal can create a compute resource and give it a role it does not hold. Whatever runs on that resource gets the role's permissions.\n\nPrerequisites:\n\n- the role trusts sagemaker.amazonaws.com\n\n## Why it matters\n\nEscalation paths turn a limited identity into an administrator. Attackers who obtain any credential look for exactly this permission combination; defenders rarely notice it in policy reviews because each statement looks reasonable on its own.\n\n## Attack chain\n\n1. The principal creates a new resource (`sagemaker:CreateNotebookInstance`) and passes a privileged role that trusts `sagemaker.amazonaws.com`.\n2. Code it controls runs with the role's credentials.\n\n## Vulnerable example\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"iam:PassRole\",\n        \"sagemaker:CreateNotebookInstance\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Fixed example\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": \"iam:PassRole\",\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:iam::111111111111:role/app-runtime-*\",\n      \"Condition\": {\n        \"StringEquals\": {\n          \"iam:PassedToService\": \"sagemaker.amazonaws.com\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"sagemaker:CreateNotebookInstance\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Remediation\n\nScope iam:PassRole to the roles the caller must pass and add \"Condition\": {\"StringEquals\": {\"iam:PassedToService\": \"sagemaker.amazonaws.com\"}} only for those roles.\n\n## References\n\n- https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_passrole.html\n- https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/266.html\n- pathfinding.cloud: [sagemaker-001](https://pathfinding.cloud/paths/aws/sagemaker-001)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
